 # ProcessManager: add PTY spawn mode via @lydell/node-pty
 
-
+Add PTY allocation support to the ProcessManager for use cases that require pseudo-terminal semantics (color output, interactive programs, terminal size detection).
+
+## Context
+
+AGENT-15 implemented the background process framework MVP using `child_process.spawn()`. This works for most background tasks (builds, test watchers, etc.) but doesn't support PTY-specific features:
+- Color output from programs that detect non-TTY stdout
+- Interactive programs requiring terminal control
+- Terminal size detection and viewport awareness
+- Programs that behave differently in PTY vs. pipe mode
+
+## Scope
+
+- Add `mode: 'pty' | 'child'` option to `SpawnOptions`
+- Implement PTY adapter using `@lydell/node-pty` (prebuilt binaries, no compiler needed)
+- Support PTY-specific options: cols, rows, terminal type
+- Handle PTY unified output stream (no separate stdout/stderr)
+- Update tools to expose PTY mode option
+- Tests for PTY spawn mode
+
+## References
+
+- `.sandpiper/docs/openclaw-process-supervisor-investigation.md` — PTY adapter design research
+- `packages/core/src/process-manager.ts` — current implementation (child mode only)
+- AGENT-15 — original background framework (completed without PTY)
+- SHR-71 — PTY adapter for shell_relay (WONTFIX — not needed for shell_relay)
+
